    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="1213" n="1063" xml:id="pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4960/77.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Yenikeny</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-06-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 15,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>No. 48. Beferring to the fifth demand in his telegram of April 10, reports the
                    satisfactory settlement of the Manoukian case,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d415-f1"/>
                    which has been so long pending, and which involved the recognition by the
                    Sublime Porte of our consular courts as alone competent to decide as to legal
                    heirs of an American citizen.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
